      "latency_ms": 10335.6,
      "prompt_tokens": 25,
      "completion_tokens": 1151,
      "output": "\n\nWater is a chemical substance with the molecular formula **H₂O**, consisting of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom. It is one of the most essential and unique substances on Earth, vital for life and playing a critical role in natural processes. Here's a breakdown of its key characteristics:\n\n### **Chemical and Physical Properties**\n- **Molecular Structure**: Water is a **polar molecule**, meaning it has a partial positive charge on the hydrogen atoms and a partial negative charge on the oxygen atom. This polarity allows water molecules to form **hydrogen bonds**, which give water its distinctive properties.\n- **States of Matter**: At standard temperature and pressure, water exists as a **liquid**, but it can also transition into **solid (ice)** or **gas (water vapor)**. Notably, **ice is less dense than liquid water**, which is why it floats—critical for aquatic ecosystems in cold climates.\n- **Unique Properties**: \n  - **High specific heat capacity**: Water absorbs and releases heat slowly, helping regulate temperature in organisms and the environment.\n  - **Cohesion and adhesion**: Water molecules stick to each other (cohesion) and to other surfaces (adhesion), enabling processes like capillary action in plants.\n  - **Solvent capabilities**: Often called the \"universal solvent,\" water dissolves many substances, facilitating chemical reactions in living systems.\n\n### **Biological Importance**\n- **Life-Sustaining**: All known forms of life depend on water. It acts as a **solvent** for biochemical reactions, a **transport medium** for nutrients and waste, and a **temperature regulator** (e.g., through sweating in humans).\n- **Human Body**: The human body is about **60% water**, with fluids like blood, saliva, and cellular fluids relying on water for function.\n\n### **Environmental Role**\n- **Hydrological Cycle**: Water cycles through Earth's systems via **evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and runoff**, sustaining ecosystems and weather patterns.\n- **Habitat**: Oceans, lakes, rivers, and groundwater support diverse life forms and shape landscapes.\n\n### **Other Key Facts**\n- **Tasteless, Odorless, and Colorless**: Pure water has no taste or smell and appears clear.\n- **Variants**: Water exists in different forms, such as **freshwater** (rivers, lakes), **saltwater** (oceans), and **ice** (glaciers, polar caps).\n\nIn summary, water is a simple yet extraordinary molecule whose unique properties make it indispensable for life, environmental stability, and countless natural and industrial processes."
    },
